{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many points of inflection does the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/641e9e24a2b373677e1f0aa2067b4147fba047a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = (x-\\cos x)(x+\\cos x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" /> have on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6db8d0f14374fc4a15dcadad7fdfe6689fca145.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 2\\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51828f450c88d2aed8a9dafff06184248375934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1  \\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 0  \\quad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4  \\quad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{infinitely many} \\quad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"385\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By difference of squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/989800dcffd609993428c0c65f257b22bad6790a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^{2} - \\cos^{2}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" />. Points of inflection occur when the second derivative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc8b3f74bcf7c07fc0bb6e488182f87b42dc507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"19\" /> changes signs, so we calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c55e09befcf52668c0b113833631099229e9500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39; = 2x + 2\\cos x \\sin x = 2x + \\sin 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"281\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb9c7a3d767a8558b1a6030cf92d666d6ad0c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39; = 2 + 2\\cos 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378ef709522ce9a9d91b19214485ae2669967b0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39; = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"19\" />, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\t2 + 2 \\cos 2x &amp;= 0\\\\\n\t\\cos 2x &amp;= -1\\\\\n\t2x &amp;= \\pi + 2\\pi k\\\\\n\tx &amp;= \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi k\n\\end{align*}\nfor every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/29238f408d8cb5806f06cc03446dde0084ffe09d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. We can calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f0831ef6a6a2dac4c600f2a2c9aa0e283e38dcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39;&#39; = -4\\sin 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10ac4e951e07c32af7fa2e6cc0057d261a2ae00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sin \\left( 2\\cdot \\left( \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + \\pi k \\right) \\right) = 4\\sin (\\pi + 2\\pi k)= 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"332\" height=\"35\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc8b3f74bcf7c07fc0bb6e488182f87b42dc507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"19\" /> does not change signs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30ca02a6cd2fb22230d593a41d3426963305f3eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/641e9e24a2b373677e1f0aa2067b4147fba047a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = (x-\\cos x)(x+\\cos x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e790cd0f18ffd78e62e12077df381843fdeb4ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> points of inflection.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb9c7a3d767a8558b1a6030cf92d666d6ad0c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39; = 2 + 2\\cos 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" /> as in Solution 1. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/177ac19f908ac269d4958855bf9a8ace9e546fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 \\le \\cos 2x \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12d935f531afb9998ced9a4964d33ec8761cc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le 2 + 2\\cos 2x \\le 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"159\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc8b3f74bcf7c07fc0bb6e488182f87b42dc507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"19\" /> never changes signs, so the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/641e9e24a2b373677e1f0aa2067b4147fba047a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = (x-\\cos x)(x+\\cos x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e790cd0f18ffd78e62e12077df381843fdeb4ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> points of inflection.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_Schoo